{
    "family": "conv2d_fprop_gfx1151",
    "op_kind": "conv_fprop",
    "arch": "gfx1151",
    "dtype": [
        "f16",
        "bf16"
    ],
    "_comment": "Runtime-generic 2-D forward-convolution (implicit-GEMM) family for gfx1151 (WMMA, wave32, groups==1). Every kernel is FULLY dynamic: one .co per tile config serves ANY conv shape via partial-tile boundary masking (parity with rmsnorm2d_dynamic/layernorm2d_dynamic, applied to conv). The ConvFpropAdapter publishes dtype/groups/C/K plus the raw geometry + derived M/N_gemm/K_gemm; each kernel gates on dtype+groups+C/K-alignment only. Grid = ceil_div(N_gemm,tile_n) x ceil_div(M,tile_m). ABI = A,B,D + A_bytes,B_bytes,D_bytes + N,C,K,Hi,Wi,R,S,sH,sW,pH,pW,dH,dW (all i32). A CDNA arch ships its own .co + family.json entry with matching constraints -- zero C++ change.",
    "kernels": [
        {
            "symbol": "conv_igemm_fprop_dyn_fp16_t64x64x64_w2x2_a16x16x16_mem_default",
            "co_file": "conv_igemm_fprop_dyn_fp16_t64x64x64_w2x2_a16x16x16_mem_default.co",
            "_comment": "Fully runtime-generic forward conv: ALL geometry (N,C,K,Hi,Wi,R,S,stride,pad,dilation) is read from i32 args; only the tile config is baked. No shape 'equals'/'multiple_of' on spatial dims -- partial tiles are masked. C/K are constrained multiple_of vec for the channel-contiguous vectorized loads. Serves any 2-D fprop shape; the tuner picks the winning tile config per problem.",
            "constraints": {
                "dtype": {
                    "equals": "f16"
                },
                "groups": {
                    "equals": 1
                },
                "C": {
                    "min": 1,
